@project:P{br=~199:Evaluate whether candidate.png is ready to become the baseline sprite for the rest of the robot family. The agreed visual identity is reference.png. Inputs are 32x32 RGBA sprites in the project root.;in=[@i-canvas,@i-palette,@i-alpha,@i-view,@i-identity,@i-identity-features,@i-destination];nm=~28:Robot family baseline review;ow=@user;sc=[@s-assignment,@s-reference]}
@q-baseline-fitness:Q{ck=~226:The sprite is a sound starting point to derive sibling robots from: its identity features are the reference's, and any asymmetry present is a deliberate design feature rather than a dropped element that siblings would inherit.;dm=other;md=visual;nm=~30:Fitness as the family baseline;so=[@s-assignment];wh=@actor}
@q-identity:Q{ck=~321:Inspected enlarged beside reference.png, the candidate carries the agreed identity: both head antennae present, both eyes present, and the silhouette bilaterally symmetric about the sprite centre as in the reference. A feature the reference has and the candidate drops is a failure even when colours and dimensions match.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~34:Identity fidelity to reference.png;so=[@s-reference,@s-assignment];wh=@actor}
@q-mechanical:Q{ck=~140:32x32 RGBA; every visible pixel is one of #25354A, #56B5BC or #F4DDA2; zero fractional-alpha pixels; exactly one connected opaque component.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~31:Mechanical contract conformance;so=[@s-assignment];wh=@actor}
